#: ../../index.rst:1
msgid "Guidedog builds documentation websites and PDF books from reStructuredText and Markdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:5
msgid "Guidedog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:10
msgid "Write once. Explain well. Publish on the web and on paper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:14
msgid "Guidedog builds a documentation website and a PDF book from the same reStructuredText or Markdown files. You write the text once; Guidedog keeps the two editions in step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:20
msgid "`Read the manual <manual_>`_ `Download <download_>`_ `Source code <source_>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:31
msgid "A plain text file goes in. Guidedog makes a web page and a book page from it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:34
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:39
msgid "**A website.** Pages with navigation, search, highlighted code, and light and dark themes, from Jinja templates you can change as much as you like."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:41
msgid "**A PDF book.** Chapters, cross-references, figures, tables, footnotes, and an index, set by Typst with hyphenation for each language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:43
msgid "**reStructuredText and Markdown.** Directives, roles, toctrees, and cross-references work as Sphinx users expect, and MyST Markdown can sit next to them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:45
msgid "**Translations.** Gettext catalogs carry a project into other languages. Chinese, Japanese, Korean, and Hindi text is laid out correctly on screen and on paper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:47
msgid "**Diagrams, math, and API pages.** Graphviz diagrams, LaTeX equations, and Odin API reference read from source code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:49
msgid "**Clear errors.** A message says what is wrong, where, and how to fix it. A failed build leaves the last good site in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:53
msgid "One program"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:56
msgid "Guidedog is a single binary. You do not need a Python environment, a LaTeX installation, or separate theme and extension packages. Configuration is a TOML file, and templates are plain files in your project that you can edit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:60
msgid "Some things still come from outside. Guidedog can be built with Typst and Graphviz inside it; a build without them uses the ``typst`` and Graphviz programs installed on your system. On Linux and macOS it also uses a few system libraries, such as libcurl."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:65
msgid "Write it, see both"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:68
msgid "On the left is reStructuredText. On the right is what Guidedog made of it on this page. The PDF builder sets the same lines as a book page."
msgstr ""

