#: ../../index.rst:117
msgid "Get started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:120
msgid "Download the archive for your system from the `latest release <download_>`_, put ``guidedog`` on your ``PATH``, and create a project:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:123
msgid ""
"guidedog quickstart docs\n"
"guidedog build html docs\n"
"guidedog build pdf docs\n"
"guidedog serve docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:130
msgid "``quickstart`` writes ``conf.toml``, ``index.rst``, and templates you can edit. ``serve`` rebuilds the site while you write. The `tutorial <manual-tutorial_>`_ walks through a first project. To build Guidedog from source, install Odin and follow the `instructions in the repository <build_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:136
msgid "Design discussions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:139
msgid "Guidedog's design decisions are written down as numbered discussions: the problem, the alternatives, the decision, and the evidence. You can read each one on the web or download it as a PDF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:143
msgid "Your project can keep its own discussions the same way, with ``dsc``, which comes with Guidedog. The `manual <manual-discussions_>`_ shows how."
msgstr ""

